{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdPpwdtmbVtrzWKRM33WV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about a ROS 2 issue where they're subscribing to a topic `/camera/image_raw` but not receiving any messages, even though `ros2 topic hz` shows the topic is being published at 30 Hz.\n\nThis is a common ROS 2 issue. Let me think about the most likely causes:\n\n1. **QoS Mismatch**: The most common cause is a Quality of Service (QoS) mismatch between the publisher and subscriber. In ROS 2, if the publisher and subscriber have incompatible QoS settings, they won't connect. For image topics, this is very common because:\n   - Image topics often use a sensor data QoS profile (BEST_EFFORT, small history)\n   - Default subscription often uses DEFAULT or RELIABLE QoS\n   - These don't match, so no messages flow\n\n2. **Callback signature issue**: If using Python/C++, wrong callback signature won't call the callback\n\n3. **Namespace issues**: Topic names not matching (though they said `ros2 topic hz` works)\n\n4. **Node initialization issues**: Not spinning the executor\n\n5. **Wrong topic name or typo**: But `ros2 topic hz` shows it's being published\n\nGiven the symptoms - the topic exists and has data (verified by `ros2 topic hz`), the node compiles and starts - this strongly points to **QoS mismatch**.\n\nFor camera image topics, the publisher typically publishes with a sensor data QoS profile which uses BEST_EFFORT reliability. If the subscriber uses the default which is RELIABLE, they won't match.\n\nHowever, I should provide practical troubleshooting steps. The user hasn't shared their code, so I should ask for it or provide the most likely solution.\n\nActually, let me reconsider - the user is asking \"What's wrong?\" without sharing code. I should ask for their subscription code to diagnose properly. But I can give them the top suspect immediately.\n\nThe skill `ros2-perception` is available, but that's more about specific perception packages. \n\nSince the topic is actively publishing data but the subscriber isn't receiving it, QoS incompatibility is the prime suspect—camera drivers typically use BEST_EFFORT while default subscriptions expect RELIABLE. I should ask for their subscription code to confirm, but can immediately suggest checking QoS settings and using the sensor data profile as the fix.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6593,"cache_read_input_tokens":12851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6593},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60f9895a-8600-4bee-bf5d-900108ddaab4","uuid":"fbba9df6-15d4-4aa3-8469-7cb1eb96e7de","timestamp":"2026-07-26T01:48:24.106Z","request_id":"req_011CdPpwdA7ooZP3oQy9xw54"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdPpwdtmbVtrzWKRM33WV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is almost certainly a **QoS (Quality of Service) mismatch**. Camera topics typically publish with sensor data QoS (BEST_EFFORT reliability), but subscriptions default to RELIABLE. They won't connect.\n\n**To verify and fix:**\n\nCheck what QoS the publisher is using:\n```bash\nros2 topic info /camera/image_raw --verbose\n```\n\nLook for the \"Publisher profile name\" and \"Reliability\" settings. If it's BEST_EFFORT, update your subscriber to match:\n\n**C++:**\n```cpp\nauto qos = rclcpp::SensorDataQoS();\nsubscription_ = this->create_subscription<sensor_msgs::msg::Image>(\n    \"/camera/image_raw\", qos, [this](const sensor_msgs::msg::Image::SharedPtr msg) {\n        // callback\n    });\n```\n\n**Python:**\n```python\nqos = rclpy.qos.QoSProfile(\n    reliability=rclpy.qos.ReliabilityPolicy.BEST_EFFORT,\n    history=rclpy.qos.HistoryPolicy.KEEP_LAST,\n    depth=1)\nself.subscription = self.create_subscription(\n    Image, '/camera/image_raw', self.callback, qos)\n```\n\nShare your subscription code if this doesn't fix it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6593,"cache_read_input_tokens":12851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6593},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60f9895a-8600-4bee-bf5d-900108ddaab4","uuid":"9cc64746-4c41-427c-9a62-204a84d635a2","timestamp":"2026-07-26T01:48:25.953Z","request_id":"req_011CdPpwdA7ooZP3oQy9xw54"}
